Notes:
- probe recall counts only probes that actually ran and compares exact reader identity (service, version, route_id, store_id, record_id); a probe of another version of the same service is not the obligation the proposed fleet carries, and a call rejected by the allowlist does not count.
- `established PASS` counts required obligation keys probed with PASS; `unknown probes` counts required keys probed with any other status (UNKNOWN, harness error, timeout).
- `evidence supports claim` says whether the run's claimed disposition is backed by its own observed probe outcomes: BOUNDED_PASS needs a PASS on every required key; BLOCKED needs an observed FAIL on the proposed fleet; NEEDS_EVIDENCE is supported only when the expected disposition is also NEEDS_EVIDENCE. `unsupported BOUNDED_PASS` is reported separately from `false BOUNDED_PASS` (which keeps its meaning: claimed BOUNDED_PASS, oracle disagrees), and oracle-consistent runs additionally require a supported claim.
- a saved product receipt counts as evidence for an obligation only when the obligation's hash is the canonical hash of its tuple and the receipt carries exactly that tuple; anything else is reported as a note and is not evidence. A BOUNDED_PASS claim from a report that lists evidence gaps is unsupported. Where a key was probed more than once (retries), the fold is FAIL > unresolved > PASS, so a later PASS never hides an earlier FAIL or UNKNOWN.
- `proposed cart route/store x 2002 probes` requires every applicable route/store of the proposed cart version on saved-cart-2002; multiple applicable keys report their individual coverage.
- disposition for a fleet with no oracle case is derived from the oracle's per-reader predictions plus manifest gaps, and the row says so.
